          "quote": "Data Center segment revenue was $6.7 billion, up 107% year-over-year, driven by strong demand for AMD EPYC™ processors and AMD Instinct™ GPUs."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "One synthetic vendor report has eight respondents, not eight verified independent sources; identities, shared orders and upstream information overlap are unknown.",
    "Rising custom share refers to unspecified new rack orders, not measured incremental accelerator dollars; customer identity, pricing, denominator and delivery year are unquantified.",
    "A single planner's 2027 power constraint does not establish a 2026 capex change or a dated supplier shipment/acceptance delay.",
    "Stable 20–30 week neocloud lead times lack a prior comparable check and may describe allocations or existing orders; they cannot be assigned to Big Four procurement.",
    "Rack delivery, revenue acceptance and energization may occur at different times. Larger orders can coexist with staged power deployment and construction spending.",
    "AMD availability and combined EPYC/Instinct segment revenue do not quantify GPU-only sales or support changing the consensus-anchored base.",
    "NVIDIA's expected November 18 report date remains unconfirmed; the attempted Microsoft FY26 annual-report fetch returned 404."
  ],
  "catalysts": [
    "Late October 2026: hyperscaler results and capex/2027 commentary; seek server/custom-silicon mix, power-ready capacity and deployment schedules.",
    "Before November's NVIDIA report: a comparable channel check with order cohorts, delivery dates, respondent-overlap methodology and lead-time baselines.",
    "2026-11-18, expected/unconfirmed: NVIDIA Q3 FY27 versus $103bn Data Center; Q4 outlook versus own $128bn and required $129.86bn.",
    "Early November 2026, expected: AMD Q3 GPU-only revenue and recognized Helios shipments; availability alone is insufficient.",
    "January-February 2027: capex guides and commissioned-power schedules to test conversion of larger 2027 rack orders."
  ],
  "disconfirming_evidence": [
    "The channel's larger 2027 order indications and stable NVIDIA lead times argue against treating the report as evidence of a current demand collapse or newly lengthening procurement delay.",
    "NVIDIA's August 26 release named Rubin racks running at Google Cloud and Microsoft Azure; custom adoption does not eliminate NVIDIA deployments.",
    "The channel offers no quantified custom share; the upside reduction could prove too cautious if incremental dollars still favor NVIDIA.",
    "A planner's power constraint challenges the vendor's assertion that only share, rather than volume, is in question: energized capacity may be delayed even with intact orders.",
    "New-order evidence concerns largely 2027 and therefore gives limited grounds to change the calendar 2026 base."
  ],
