    "finding": "The report is a distinct source family claiming fresh October interviews and adds an apparently incremental order-mix observation; anonymous respondents and order overlap prevent verifying independence. No earlier eligible channel check was found. Prior AWS primary disclosures independently establish Trainium deployment and 2027 capacity commitments, but do not validate the two unnamed clouds or incremental dollar share. Power can constrain energized deployment despite larger orders, as one 2027 planner reports; no dated shipment, acceptance or revenue slip is established. Stable neocloud lead times provide no evidence of deterioration. Conditionally, new orders placed October 1–8 at 20–30 weeks would fall February 18–May 6, 2027; this is arithmetic, not a disclosed delivery schedule. Cut only NVIDIA bull share 0.5 point as a persistence-confidence haircut; hold 2026 base/capex, Q3 $103bn, own Q4 $128bn and AMD. Public confirmation of power timing remains unresolved; Microsoft annual-report fetch returned 404.",
    "status": "partially_answered"
  },
  "open_questions": [
    "Will H2 capex reach MSFT cash PP&E $83.322bn, GOOGL PP&E purchases $99.402bn, AMZN gross purchases $116.589bn and META inclusive capex $86.58bn? Late-October Q3 results and updated guides will test these run rates.",
    "How much of each capex dollar is accelerator systems versus prices, buildings and power? Customer mix and cash/lease reconciliations in late-October results and NVIDIA's November report would move mix.",
    "What is Big Four's actual share of NVIDIA revenue after customer recasting and indirect AI-cloud purchases? Named-customer/cohort definitions in the expected November report would test the held 45% base.",
    "Will NVIDIA Q3 FY27 Data Center reach $103bn, and will Q4 support own $128bn versus required $129.86bn? Expected 2026-11-18 results/guide will answer; company confirmation is still needed for the date and no Q3 segment consensus was supplied.",
    "What is AMD's recognized 2026 Instinct revenue, excluding EPYC, and when do Meta/Azure Helios plans convert? A GPU-only disclosure and shipment timing in early-November AMD Q3 results would permit a variant from $14bn.",
    "Will 2027 capex guides rise and AWS margins remain resilient after depreciation/power costs? Late-October commentary and January-February 2027 full-year guides will test persistence.",
    "Are the channel respondents independent, which two clouds are involved, and is custom share measured in units, racks or dollars? Vendor methodology/order-cohort detail or matching customer disclosures before the late-October/November results would validate the incremental-share signal.",
    "Does power readiness defer identifiable 2027 racks, supplier acceptance or merely energization, and are orders cancelled or staged? Company power-ready dates and revised deployment schedules in late-October results/2027 guidance would establish a dated slip.",
    "Do stable 20–30 week neocloud lead times apply to new orders or existing allocations, and how do they compare with a prior check? A comparable follow-up check before November's NVIDIA report would distinguish normal procurement cadence from new delay."
  ],
